# Chapter 1 Project
<img src="https://images.code.org/d360461271d0f8d230673bc48cf12ea2-image-1777324109530.07.07 PM.png" alt="A website with a resume for a user named Alana" width="300px" style="float:right; margin-left:20px;padding-right: 10px;">

<a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/ai-discoveries-2026/units/3/lessons/14" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lesson Plan</a>

Chapter 1 of the Web Development unit concludes with a multi-lesson project where students will use the skills they have learned throughout the unit to create and design a web page for a user. They will be able to choose from several different users with distinct needs to style their web page.

Students begin their project by using the Problem Solving Process to help them determine how they will organize the content of a user’s web page. Students then use CSS classes and flexbox to organize their user’s web page in Web Lab. Optionally, after engaging in a formal feedback process, they may change their web pages based on feedback before reflecting on their process.

## Project Options

Read over the options below, then open the project resources for the option of your choice.

**Option 1 - Easy:** Students add classes and flexbox to web page content that is already organized with `<div>` elements. Choose this option if you don’t have time available to allow your students to either alter the code that will be brought over from the Lesson 10 mini-project or build a new web page for a new user from scratch.

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Option 1 Project Resources</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 5px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:5px;">

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1llotpD2fYz5CdLkEiQb-ouO1bKtobBh2UyYGfh0uSH8/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 1 Activity Guide</a><br>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MEan92ixZ7aLrRMjUu1h8L0bJg2DfeHf1KX_rWANYmo/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 1 Project Rubric</a>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T0-5a1gYerxs4rfu6ktlZpzBnp2NaN341CHPUP0KZQs/edit?usp=sharing" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 1 Project Student Checklist</a>
</div></details>
<br>

**Option 2 - Intermediate**: Students add `div` tags, classes, and Flexbox to the webpage they styled for Lesson 10. Choose this option if your students are up for the challenge and you have the extra time (possibly 2 days) to allow students to shift their HTML code, iterating on their HTML to make their page look as their user requests.

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Option 2 Project Resources</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 5px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:5px;">

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VwEzTDsVaIi8oYILUxdUeEe8DzH00hRpgKvwXUQ6hB4/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 2 Activity Guide</a>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1h4LafqbTvxdpygc1jmpNuQ_ngxLDIuoKbIuk2K-5Fp4/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 2 Project Rubric</a>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rxz-8GAoLLJn8zsy_NmwZ5UJ7WND1qzKKxefbxa6zbg/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 2 Project Student Checklist</a>
</div></details>
<br>

**Option 3 - Challenging**: Students create a webpage for a new user from scratch. Choose this option if you have at least 2-3 days to dedicate to this project and would like students to have the experience of building a webpage from beginning to end without breaks in between the process.

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Option 3 Project Resources</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 5px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:5px;">

* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lEq51w4Ldm4xetEsoq9WIMTDbyhvIp-LknibXGFmCRg/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 3 Activity Guide</a>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ACaiFhEAMabueHNVEYQKz8YRVHOXqKPHjpOKej8XvHU/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 3 Project Rubric</a>
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xb5xJyp2QjOrHAkm5bMMGexJWPosC-Off32-mwwL-Fg/view" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Option 3 Project Student Checklist</a>
</div></details>
<br>

## Pacing Recommendation

If you are short on time, this project can be used as way to wrap up the unit. This project can also be expanded out to include a student presentation if you have the time available. 

## Sample Student Projects

Click the images below to view the sample projects in a new tab.

